.TITLE "wsl"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Enables developers to run a GNU/Linux environment directly on Windows without the overhead of a traditional virtual machine or dual-boot setup.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**wsl**
Starts the default Linux distribution in the current terminal.
> 

**wsl --list --online**
Lists the available Linux distributions that can be installed.
> __--list__ list flag | __--online__ online source flag

**wsl --install -d Ubuntu**
Installs the specified Linux distribution.
> __--install__ install flag | __-d__ distribution flag

**wsl --update**
Manages updates to the WSL kernel and components.
> __--update__ update flag

**wsl --shutdown**
Immediately terminates all running distributions and the WSL 2 lightweight utility virtual machine.
> __--shutdown__ termination flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
WSL 2 provides full system call compatibility and increased file system performance. Use __wsl --shutdown__ to free up system resources if you are no longer using your Linux environments.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:powershell** **windows:cmd**

